{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1779229030,"nonce":"aWXrW7FwPfxBXt2exvx0DSJUmAE=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABCx22dQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/139","origin":"github"},"title":"Replace output='screen' with output='both' in BizzyBoat launch files (loses crash output today)","message":"## Problem\n\nSeveral BizzyBoat launch files declare nodes with `output='screen'`, sending stdout/stderr only to the launch terminal. When a node crashes silently on startup, the actual exception text is **only available in the launch terminal scrollback** — not in `~/.ros/log/`, not in `/rosout` (if it dies before publishing), not in any rosbag.\n\nThis bit us in [#135 (2026-05-19 deployment)](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/135) — `mikrotik_monitor` and `teltonika_monitor` both crashed at startup on salmon (see [ros2_network_monitor#23](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_network_monitor/issues/23)). The actual crash reason is still pending because the only place it landed is `pts/5` scrollback on salmon.\n\n## Proposed fix\n\nAudit BizzyBoat launch files (under `bizzyboat_project11/launch/` and any included launch fragments) and replace `output='screen'` with one of:\n\n- **`output='both'`** — visible in launch terminal AND written to `~/.ros/log/`. Best for dev convenience + ops recoverability.\n- **`output='log'`** (the ROS 2 default) — log files only. Cleaner terminal during ops; everything still recoverable.\n- Drop the kwarg entirely (uses default, which is `log`).\n\n## Audit scope\n\n- `bizzyboat_project11/launch/operator_core_launch.py` (includes `network_monitor_operator_launch.py`)\n- `bizzyboat_project11/launch/network_monitor_operator_launch.py`\n- Any boat-side launch files declaring `output='screen'`\n- Other launch files in the workspace? — out of scope here; this issue is BizzyBoat-side only.\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe dev convenience of `output='screen'` is real, but the ops cost when a node dies silently is real too — we lose the ability to root-cause from anything other than a still-alive terminal. `output='both'` keeps the dev visibility while making the failure recoverable.\n\n## Related\n\n- [ros2_network_monitor#23](https://github.com/rolker/ros2_network_monitor/issues/23) — the symptom that surfaced this\n- Today's deployment: [#135](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/135), salmon log §12\n\nPart of #135\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}